# bat configuration — one CLI argument per line.
#
# Default+ is not built into bat, so the theme is vendored as
# themes/default-plus.tmTheme. bat only picks a theme file up from a compiled
# cache, so after a fresh `./install.sh bat` (or any edit to it) run:
#
#     bat cache --build
#
# `bat --list-themes` should then show `default-plus`. Note bat names a *user*
# theme after its filename, not the `name` key inside the plist, and a wrong
# value is silent — bat falls back to its built-in Monokai default and prints
# orange rather than erroring. Verify after any rename.
#
# The file is hand-written against docs/palette.md; Default+ has no upstream
# tmTheme to copy. Roles follow Xcode, so comments are green and strings are
# red — that inversion is deliberate, see docs/palette.md.

--theme="default-plus"

# Line numbers, git modification markers and a header per file, but no grid.
--style="numbers,changes,header"

# Only page when the output doesn't fit; keep colors and let bat's default
# less flags through.
--paging=auto
